    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nClaude Code Plan mode is described as **\u201cPlanning mode, no actual tool execution.\u201d** In native ChatUI QA it executed tools and persisted a plan file under `~/.claude/plans`, outside the session worktree, even though the prompt explicitly prohibited tools and file changes.\n\n**Source:** [ChatUI QA and regression harness PR #4419](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4419)  \n**Reported by:** Dhruv Sharma via local native-Electron QA  \n**Analyzed against:** `d71acca1e13ddd9ab3a01a43f029853686f4c693`; relevant paths rechecked on `04b676c9abd2fac4505081b0c099e079a30bde57`  \n**Environment:** macOS arm64, source-built `ao` (`dev`), verified daemon on port 3001  \n**Priority:** P1 \u2014 the UI presents a false safety boundary  \n**Confidence:** High \u2014 reproduced natively, filesystem side effect captured, and rendering/forwarding path traced\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Open a Claude Code session in ChatUI.\n2. Select **Plan** in the permission-mode menu.\n3. Prompt it to produce a plan while explicitly saying not to execute tools or modify files.\n4. Observe Read/Write activity and a new Markdown plan under `~/.claude/plans`.\n5. Deny the later \u201cReady to code?\u201d prompt; the plan file already exists.\n\n## Expected\n\nEither AO enforces a genuine no-tool/no-write boundary, or the menu truthfully explains provider-native Plan mode, including possible file inspection, tool use, and provider-owned plan files outside the worktree.\n\n## Actual\n\nAO renders an absolute \u201cno actual tool execution\u201d promise while passing the provider mode through without enforcing that boundary.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- `backend/internal/adapters/chatdriver/acp/config_options.go:172` forwards provider descriptions.\n- `frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/TurnSettingsBar.tsx:544` renders the categorical description without qualification.\n- Mode changes are forwarded to ACP; AO does not currently impose a tool/write policy at this boundary.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nPrefer truthful provider-specific disclosure unless AO can enforce a strict read-only mode. Add a provider contract test that observes writes outside the worktree.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Plan-mode copy never promises a boundary AO does not enforce.\n- Claude-specific behavior explains provider-owned plan artifacts before selection.\n- `npm run qa:chatui -- --grep MQA-01` passes in strict mode.\n\n## Evidence\n\n![Claude Plan mode writes a plan file](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/b7d4a8dc8cf8843be42a3c0bb183e35103ccd06f/docs/qa/chatui-2026-08-25/screenshots/22-plan-mode-writes-plan-file.png)\n\n- [Full finding and expected/actual details](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/blob/b7d4a8dc8cf8843be42a3c0bb183e35103ccd06f/docs/qa/chatui-2026-08-25/manual-qa-report.md)\n- [Captured filesystem evidence](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/blob/b7d4a8dc8cf8843be42a3c0bb183e35103ccd06f/docs/qa/chatui-2026-08-25/evidence/plan-mode-created-file.md)\n\n## Related\n\n- [PR #4419](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4419) \u2014 local-only regression harness and QA evidence\n- [#3745](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/3745) \u2014 separate read-only reviewer-harness work; not a duplicate",
